    {
        "text": "Even the scorching light of the flames cannot stop Rankin from seeing what is inside the house, over Hawley's head\u2014"
    },
    {
        "text": "Flames roil and writhe as charred beams totter, cracking like the moaning of the dying."
    },
    {
        "text": "An old woman sits straight in the middle of it all."
    },
    {
        "text": "......",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Old Woman"
    },
    {
        "text": "She is sitting on the last chair without a sound. The flames are only inches from her, but they cannot touch her, as though an invisible wall is keeping them at bay."
    },
    {
        "text": "She has not a speck of ash or dust on her. Even her hair is immaculately clean. Her eyes gently shut, but at the same time she seems to be watching everything."
    },
    {
        "text": "I have cleansed their souls.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Hawley"
    },
